nio: switch to the init task map before exec

Run 602 reaches exec /sbin/launchd but fails with errno 14 (EFAULT):
the panel shows far=0xfffffff09380f000, a kernel address.  load_init_program
is called directly on the boot thread (the init thread cannot be scheduled
this early), so current_map() is kernel_map, not the init task's user map.
copyout() of the argv and copyinstr() of the filename then touch kernel
addresses as if they were user addresses -> EFAULT.

Switch the current thread to the init task's own map at the top of
load_init_program(), so scratch_addr and the execve filename land in a
real user map.  A panel mark confirms the switch.  Diagnosis only.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
index e1bd7ce..1ad597a 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -7956,6 +7956,16 @@ load_init_program(proc_t p)
 	boot_progress_stage("load_init_program enter");
 	uint32_t i;
 	int error;
+	/* nio: we run on the boot thread, whose map is kernel_map; the init
+	 * task has its own (empty) user map. Switch to it so scratch_addr and
+	 * the execve filename are real user addresses (else EFAULT). */
+	{
+		vm_map_t init_map = proc_get_task_raw(p)->map;
+		if (init_map != VM_MAP_NULL) {
+			(void) vm_map_switch(init_map);
+			nio_emark("\nnio: exec: switched to init map");
+		}
+	}
 	vm_map_t map = current_map();
 	mach_vm_offset_t scratch_addr = 0;
 	mach_vm_size_t map_page_size = vm_map_page_size(map);
